  "note": "Triennial election of the county council, 1964: polled 4 June 1964 in Lurgan and Crossmaglen; the other 18 divisions (19 seats) returned unopposed. The nominations list prints no party labels. Two seats. 3,151 ballots cast, seven spoilt; a 35.8 per cent poll. The count was held at Armagh on Friday 5 June 1964 (returning officer H. W. F. Reid). Both Unionists were the retiring members; the Armagh Guardian (11 June 1964, p. 4) spells the Independent \"Alison Bell\"."
